  "translation": "On the weekend, my family and I left home together to go to the supermarket. The supermarket was very lively with many people. We first went to the first floor and bought apples and bananas. Then we went up to the second floor, where there were clothes for sale. Mom wanted to buy a shirt, but it was too expensive, so she didn't buy it. Dad said, \"Let's go to the west side and look at other stores.\" Later, we also went to the beverage area and ran into a neighbor. She asked us what we bought, and I said we bought a lot of things. She smiled and said she often comes here too, and the things here are really cheap. Finally, we paid and went home together. On the way home, we were all very happy, and Dad said he would come again next time. I nodded and said okay."
